WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.870
Only during the full moon or new moon is the
tide low enough.

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:12.790
That's when the aquaculture farmers of Tampolo
Bay head to their enclosures to take inventory.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:17.350
Workers from the NGO Blue Ventures monitor
the animals' growth.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:22.650
This is the group that first proposed raising
sea cucumbers to the villagers ten years ago.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.860
Once the creatures reach 400 grams, they're
ready for sale.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:32.270
There are rules for maintaining the enclosures.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:34.860
We devised them with the farmers.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:40.270
For example, no one may enter another farmer's
enclosure without his or her permission.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:41.960
Fishing of any kind is banned.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.480
Crabs are the one exception.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:50.000
THEY can be caught, because otherwise they'd
eat the sea cucumbers.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.190
All these rules serve to protect the sea.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:58.670
Before aquaculture began here, hardly any
fish were left in this lagoon.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:03.059
Today there's a greater variety of fish, snails
and crabs.

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:06.720
That's because sea cucumbers act like natural
filters.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:14.500
By ingesting sand, they purify it --removing
organic waste, microalgae and bacteria.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:20.170
In a country where 70 percent of the population
lives in poverty, this village is experiencing

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:25.299
some rare prosperity... thanks to sea cucumbers.

00:01:25.299 --> 00:01:35.990
Seraphine Kiry was one of the first aquaculture
farmers here in 2009.

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:43.520
Before the sea cucumber farm started I had
no way to raise my standard of living.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:49.189
Since I got my own enclosure, I have enough
money to send my two children to school.

00:01:49.189 --> 00:01:52.780
And I've bought a few nice things for the
house.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:02:00.310
And I have a herd of goats now.

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:04.700
The farmers pay 16 cents for the newborn sea
creatures.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:09.780
But after nine months of feeding their way
through the sand, the now-mature sea cucumbers

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.959
are worth a dollar 30.

00:02:11.959 --> 00:02:16.170
In Asia and elswhere, dried sea cucumbers
are a delicacy.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:21.650
Cultivating them benefits not only the farmers,
but the entire bay and all its marine life.

